{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/307266-vampire-the-masquerade-play-by-post-forum-gehenna-by-night","id":307266,"title":"Vampire: The Masquerade Play-by-Post forum - Gehenna by Night","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-09T01:46:33-08:00","id":307266,"title":"Vampire: The Masquerade Play-by-Post forum - Gehenna by Night","content":"Hey! Just wanted to share a new pbp forum that's starting up. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://w11.zetaboards.com/Gehenna_by_Night/index/\" target=\"_blank\">http://w11.zetaboards.com/Gehenna_by_Night/index/<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/kCyEUpD.png?1\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> <br /> What is Gehenna by Night?<br /> G to the B to the N is a Play by Post roleplaying forum set in the Final Nights of Vampire: The Masquerade. Players assume the role of their own characters who, through their own written interactions as well as those of others who drive the plot as Storytellers, create the ongoing story of the forum. The main purpose is provide a creative writing outlet in a slightly different way than traditional fan fiction or roleplaying forums. <br /> <br /> The player driven story<br /> <br /> To help drive the ongoing story, players may assume the role of the storyteller to provide other players with a cohesive and directed storyline. It may contain any elements, characters, or events that they wish as long as they don\u2019t conflict with the forum\u2019s few rules. If a player says they have a great idea for a plot about a haunted taco bell, they don\u2019t even need to ask permission to run it; they simply log into the storyteller account and start writing. In this way, characters may exist in a dynamic world that changes around them rather than stagnates because the only people approved to write plotlines don\u2019t want to or can\u2019t for whatever reason. On occasion, I will also be assuming that role to direct the story of the forum as a whole, although likely only for major changes. I leave everything else in the hands of the community to shape itself.<br /> <br /> The player driven game<br /> <br /> To help keep the game fresh and unpredictable, players are given the opportunity to essentially treat the forum as their character\u2019s sandbox. They may pursue whatever goals they want to and they will be able to measure their progress or failure with tangible assets. If a player wants to claim a domain for their own, they will be rewarded with an appropriate value of the domain background trait if they are successful. If they want to let their sect use it or enforce draconian law within it, they may. The can even reward it to their supporters if they want to. Or, players may simply hang out and interact with the other characters and their players; a fly on the wall who collects or trades gossip, and so on. It's really up to the player's determination what their character is driven to do with their immortality. <br /> <br /> The player driven community<br /> <br /> To help ensure that players are satisfied with the forum and the game, they may at any time generate discussion to make changes to it. Aside from a non-negotiable policy about abuse and harassment, Gehenna by Night is completely democratic. Players simply talk to each other and decide with a vote what change they would like to make, if any. This is probably the most radical difference between Gehenna by Night and other forums, but I feel like it\u2019s a necessary process to make certain that the forum is successful and it's community is happy with the game.<br /> <br /> Also includes a chat box and dice roller code. Feel free to drop in and ask any questions. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> -Peace<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i43.photobucket.com/albums/e384/GrottyGilgamesh/3812c9a0-1510-4235-a3d4-1993f1a47b4b_zpsd6723580.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4266-mousegbn","name":"MouseGBN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4266_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T11:02:54-08:00","id":307611,"title":"","content":"Aaaaaand a shameless plug for the forum's current metaplot:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It started quietly at first. A subtle discomfort in the air one night, an unexplainable anxiety welling up from the ground the next. Most ignored it. They passed it off as uncertainty for the city's future; the weight of a decade of distrust that casts doubt on the Anarch Free State's grand experiment. <br /> <br /> But none of L.A.'s Kindred can rationalize it as benign, now. Not after one of their most powerful and her entire brood mysteriously vanish in a pulse of violence and madness that cascades through the city. The phenomenon is accompanied by a palpable feeling of dread, and the uncertainty of the city's political climate reaches new heights.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla, recognizing an opportunity that has come earlier than expected, claims the initiative and sends a vanguard to seize the vanished Baron's substantial domain and assets, intent to maintain their established foothold until the inner circle gathers strength to commit it's overpowering ability for diplomacy and war.<br /> <br /> The Anarch Baronies, caught flatfooted and unprepared for the invasion they denied would happen, struggles to unify after so many years of infighting. Their rivalries and distrust of one another proves their greatest obstacle, but some remain determined to rally and preserve their freedom, no matter the cost.<br /> <br /> And the Sabbat, content to play the long game, comes upon a discovery that may signify their time is running out much more drastically than they thought. The Sword of Caine scrambles to find the truth and prepare itself for what horror it has always known would come. <br /> <br /> And what of the Autarkis Nosferatu? Surely, not all have befallen the fate of their matron, yet, there are none to be found for answers. And as it goes, the Brood is the first to know something, and when they go to ground to wait out the storm, it is a sure sign that something truly terrible is coming. With so many questions about what fate is brewing, there is only one truth that is certain: the Final Nights are at last upon us. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i43.photobucket.com/albums/e384/GrottyGilgamesh/3812c9a0-1510-4235-a3d4-1993f1a47b4b_zpsd6723580.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4266-mousegbn","name":"MouseGBN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4266_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}